{"id": "EUVD-2026-108632", "enisaUuid": "bf80bd92-8fa7-394e-9a5f-7342969131de", "description": "`AesGcmCryptor.Open` passed a caller-supplied nonce straight to `cipher.AEAD.Open` without checking its length. The Go standard library **panics** rather than returning an error when a GCM nonce is not exactly `NonceSize()` bytes, so a JWE carrying a wrong-sized IV crashes the decrypting goroutine.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T08:36:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:36:53", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-keypont/gose/security/advisories/GHSA-xx6h-2jgg-93m2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89312"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "63471803-dfa9-3236-aecb-fb2c77b4c76a", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.7.3 \u22640.13.0-rc1"}, {"id": "8bd273df-b0f9-3402-8731-2d114daca6e4", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.0.0-rc4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "539f235a-dbfd-3e3c-9cc6-da886ff35326", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}